+### [Mesh Normal Rasterization with Softmax Blending](18682-mesh-normal-rasterization-with-softmax-blending.md)
+This method renders ground-truth normal maps by interpolating per-vertex normals across rasterized faces using barycentric coordinates and blending overlapping faces per pixel via a softmax function. It differs from standard hard-edge rasterization by providing smooth transitions between overlapping geometry, which is critical for training differentiable rendering pipelines where normal continuity aids gradient flow.
 
